record('lifeline-case','Lifeline: BMC staffing receipts → alleged intermediary diversion → bail responses','Prosecution alleged false staffing records and routed BMC payments through Lifeline to M.S. Consultancy and Elegant Multiservices. The court-recorded alleged gross receipt is INR324,486,784.90; BMC separately reported INR33.13crore paid for manpower. Those totals overlap and are unreconciled. The February2025 Bisure bail order questions the Dean-specific kickback and billing theory; Patkar obtained bail in July2025. No final guilt or loss finding is supplied.','lifeline',L+['lifeline-bmc-response-2023','lifeline-bail-report-2025'],caseids('lifeline'),relids('lifeline'),'alleged','investigation-case','2025-07-16','BMC denies improper procurement and says payment followed services. Bisure argued limited tenure, shared invoice checks and bed-occupancy billing; the court recorded substantial prima-facie weaknesses. Patkar’s later bail rests on custody, delay and parity, not acquittal.',['No political-friendship or party edge is inferred from newspaper descriptions.','Mirror-only court sourcing remains reported; all prosecution conduct claims are expressly alleged.','Do not treat gross receipts, claimed kickbacks, asset restraints or historical headline estimates as additive loss.','Latest retained specific outcome is16July2025 bail; a later trial disposition was not found in the bounded search.'])
record('lifeline-bisure-response','Bisure response and court’s prima-facie reservations','The bail court notes no identified requirement that the Dean physically verify every staffing count, multiple review stages, and billing based on bed occupancy. It finds the claimed INR21.6lakh benefit prima facie unsubstantiated and reports no recovery from him; partnership-deed validity and routing remain trial questions.','lifeline',L,['lh-bisure','lh-firm','lh-ed','lh-hc'],['lh-dean-allegation','lh-bisure-bail'],'reported','response','2025-02-12','Defence and judicial reservations are set out in §§13,20–22; the order grants conditional bail.',['Bail observations are not final acquittal or a ruling that every Lifeline invoice was valid.'])
record('lifeline-bmc-response','BMC denies procurement wrongdoing and supplies its payment total','BMC’s reported21January2023 response says Lifeline supplied manpower after due process and rate negotiation, and bills were paid after services. Its INR33.13crore total comprises INR3.36crore NSCI and INR29.77crore Dahisar. The response disputes a political INR100crore allegation; that figure is not treated as proved loss.','lifeline',['lifeline-bmc-response-2023'],['lh-bmc','lh-firm'],['lh-contract','lh-receipts-response'],'reported','response','2023-01-21','Municipal response is retained as attributed counter-evidence, not independent clearance by a court.',['No reconciliation explaining the difference from court-recorded prosecution receipts is available.'])
record('lifeline-patkar-status','Patkar bail: custody, trial delay and parity','The Hindu reports that the HighCourt granted Patkar conditional bail16July2025, considering nearly two years’ custody, trial not yet commenced and parity with a co-accused. This changes custody status without deciding the laundering charge.','lifeline',['lifeline-bail-report-2025'],['lh-patkar','lh-gupta','lh-hc'],['lh-patkar-bail'],'reported','response','2025-07-16','Reported judicial relief and trial-stage limits attached to every Lifeline edge.',['No final trial verdict or later custody change was located.'])
record('scholarship-case','Haridwar scholarships: named societies, account routing and provisional attachment','ED’s15June2026 release traces post-matric scholarship funds through DSWO processing to three named institutions and student-name accounts. Approximately INR27.98crore total disbursements comprise INR19.74crore direct institution credits and INR8.24crore student-name credits. ED alleges INR138,353,060 in the adverse table and approximately INR13.83crore in proceeds/attached assets. The table deduplicates2,895students; it is not a comparable claim denominator for6,208claims.','scholarship',S,caseids('scholarship'),relids('scholarship'),'alleged','investigation-case','2026-06-15','No specifically attributable management response, merits judgment or order confirming this sixth attachment was located in the public search. That gap is not an admission. ED says investigation continues; its five earlier complaints are case-wide, not proof that each newly named actor was charged.',['This is a named three-institution cohort, not a statewide or national fraud estimate.','FY2011–12 overlaps the6October2011 cutoff; no datewise split supports assigning the entire cohort to the window.','Approximate society components2.44+3.95+7.44crore and the attachment valuation describe overlapping proceeds; no cross-stage sum.','INR138,353,060 is the exact table total; INR13.83crore is rounded. The exact figure is not silently substituted for attachment valuation.'])
record('scholarship-response-gap','Scholarship status: agency allegation, no retrieved merits adjudication','The official record announces a sixth provisional attachment and continuing investigation. It does not identify a final court determination for this cohort or publish defendants’ replies. Searches for the named societies and management did not locate a specific response or later merits order; unrelated same-name people are excluded.','scholarship',S,['sc-ed','sc-assets','sc-manika','sc-new-tuples','sc-motherhood-soc','sc-modern-soc'],relids('scholarship'),'reported','response','2026-06-15','Response unavailable in retrieved corpus, not refusal to respond. Authentic enrollment/eligibility records and consented account-operation evidence could rebut or narrow ED’s theory.',['No adverse inference from the response gap; no conclusion that every credited student account was management-controlled.'])
record('srmf-case','SRMF: disputed authority → society-land sale → buyer freeze and SIT','ED alleges that purported society officers used forged authority and a lookalike entity/account arrangement to sell SRMF property to Singhvahini. It separately alleges knowledge and resale by a buyer director. The SupremeCourt’s12May2026 judgment orders investigation while reserving merits and protecting one specific respondent; ED reports two other persons’ arrests and buyer/director asset freezing15May. Exact sale consideration, proceeds split and frozen value are not in the admitted originals.','srmf',T+J,caseids('srmf'),relids('srmf'),'alleged','investigation-case','2026-05-15','The court records competing management lists and pending litigation; respondent2 sought FIR quashing. It preserves conditional non-coercion for Raghvendra Pratap Singh and directs independent investigation without a merits opinion. No specific public denial by the ED-arrested persons or completed SIT report was retrieved.',['ED’s allegation of buyer knowledge is not inferred from ordinary purchaser/director status.','The original registered society and alleged lookalike mechanism are separate nodes; no fake-entity registration is invented.','Court §9 confirms freehold society land, not government leasehold; no public-grant funding is inferred.','No national spiritual organisation or unrelated trust is joined through the founder’s name.','Historical2010 and early2011 allegations are labelled context; current graph status is the2025–2026 transfer/proceeding.'])
record('srmf-court-response','SRMF court boundary: rival management, investigation and individual protection','The Court notes rival office-bearer lists and pending DelhiHighCourt proceedings. It sets aside the bar on filing a police report, orders an SIT, and preserves conditional non-coercion only for respondent2 Raghvendra Pratap Singh. The Court expressly does not decide merits.','srmf',J,['sr-society','sr-raghvendra','sr-buyer','sr-sc'],['sr-sit','sr-protection','sr-raghvendra-role'],'documented','response','2026-05-12','FIR quashing was sought; the order permits investigation and gives bounded procedural protection. It is neither an acquittal nor a finding that every buyer knowingly joined forgery.',['Do not apply protection for respondent2 to different people arrested by ED three days later.'])
record('srmf-status-gap','SRMF latest retained status and missing follow-up','ED’s15May2026 statement reports arrests/remand and asset freezing; it says further investigation continues. The earlier court-directed three-month SIT deadline is not evidence a report was filed. Follow-up search did not locate the report, a later merits judgment or specific response from the ED-arrested persons.','srmf',T+J,['sr-ed','sr-mohan','sr-akash','sr-pradeep','sr-buyer'],['sr-freeze','sr-mohan-arrest','sr-akash-arrest'],'reported','response','2026-05-15','Status is bounded to retrieved documents; no continuing incarceration, absence of defence or completed confiscation is asserted.',['No private residence pins, bank numbers or unrelated personal information is reproduced.'])

# Whitespace repair is prose-only and does not modify identity or reference keys.
import re
def tidy(t):
 t=re.sub(r'(?<=[a-z])(?=[A-Z][a-z])',' ',t)
 t=re.sub(r'\b(INR|USD|PHP)(?=\d)',r'\1 ',t)
 t=re.sub(r'(?<=[A-Za-z])(?=\d)',' ',t)
 t=re.sub(r'(?<=\d)(?=[A-Za-z])',' ',t)
 t=re.sub(r'(?<=[a-z])(?=\d)',' ',t)
 return t.replace('PMLA','PMLA').replace('2025:BHC-AS:6860','2025:BHC-AS:6860')
